executive='''# S1: proposed Executive reference frame

Status: context-generation artifact only. No fictional actor has been admitted, dispatched or executed. The useful execution choice is one separately bound direct Writer; an Executive activation and an independent Reviewer are unnecessary under the supplied project configuration. This Executive document records that selection for the owner's requested inspection. [S1-10–S1-12; DIRECT; REVIEW]

The outcome is an implementation-repair candidate for `/fictional/seed-context/candidate/context_select.py` at predecessor cut `seed-r7`, preserving the requirement and accepted design `D-seed-2`. The whole bounded cone is `select_context(records, roots, budget)`, its two candidate files and the complete supplied finite input graph. The graph may contain cycles and repeated paths; unresolved standing cannot delete a required record. The input domain excludes malformed types and duplicate record IDs. [S1-01–S1-08; CONE]

Select the repair and focused in-memory falsification as the next local frontier. The Writer inherits only S1-10's reads, edits and run-result write. It must use the finite visited-set/work-queue design, preserve opaque payload and inputs, and emit the exact result shapes and refusal order. No changed requirement, design, wider repair, ticket, Git, network, installation or publication is selected. If unchanged law cannot be met in territory, return the exact obstruction to the owner; a failing candidate does not itself authorize repricing. [S1-05–S1-08, S1-10–S1-12; WORK; released stdo-work / Establish The Work Basis]

The supplied diagnosis is a hypothesis, not an observed failure/repair. The retained `seed-r7` smoke result covers one resolved leaf only. Preserve that historical evidence under its original identity; it cannot support unresolved dependency, budget, global validation or successor-candidate claims. A changed candidate invalidates direct reliance for affected claims; still-valid evidence needs an explicit applicability check. [S1-03, S1-09; REUSE]

The draft is dependency-ready by the fixture's supplied law and grant. A hypothetical execution still has to bind the exact Product Definition and accepted frame identity, verify the selected installation, identify the separately bound capable Writer and record the existing contract's admission mechanism/decision/evidence. Those concrete coordinates are not supplied. This is a pending activation binding, not a refusal to prepare the authorized documents and not a request to approve the same grant twice. [S1-10–S1-11; DIRECT; released skills / Product Basis Selection and Establish The Work Basis]

The Writer returns exact candidate identity, changed paths, actual observations, unchanged-law evidence and residuals to the owner through `/fictional/seed-context/work/run-8/RETURN.md`, then stops. A candidate and self-review do not establish acceptance, release or adoption. Closure is bounded to this run and its applicable proved obligations; no durable ticket is needed. A Reviewer context is retained inactive. It would require a newly applicable review condition or an exact owner assessment grant, a named candidate, permitted evidence/result route, severity policy and a non-author actor with applicable independence policy. [S1-09–S1-12; WORK; REVIEW; INDEPENDENCE]

| Logical node / edge | Meaning |
|---|---|
| S1-02 + S1-04–S1-08 → D-frontier | Domain, exact closure/refusals and accepted algorithm determine the bounded repair. |
| S1-10 + S1-11 + M-direct → D-frontier | One capable direct Writer may use only the inherited grant; activation identity remains to be bound. |
| S1-03 + S1-09 + M-reuse → I-evidence | Diagnosis is unproved; the old leaf smoke cannot close the repaired behavior. |
| S1-11 + M-review → D-review-inactive | Proposed review is inactive; no mandatory independent review is invented. |
| D-frontier + S1-12 + M-work → D-return | Return candidate/evidence to the owner and stop; no acceptance or publication follows. |
| M-reuse → D-return | Material subject/input/evidence change, changed bound basis or declared revising observation withdraws affected reliance. |

These node IDs match `constraint-map.json`. `+` means all listed premises are needed; `→` is a reasoned dependency, not formal proof. Missing graph edges do not remove obligations. Actual generator host context includes injected general instructions and memory summary; no memory files or excluded arms were read, and no enforced isolation is claimed.

'''+sources
worker='''# S1: proposed direct Writer recipient context

Status: proposed, unactivated. This is the requested Worker document, but the supplied accepted frame selects one direct Writer. Apply released `stdo-work` to the existing S1-10 grant and S1-11 frame. Before any hypothetical subject read/effect, bind the exact Product Definition, verified immutable basis, accepted frame, `seed-r7` checkpoint, capable actor and actual admission evidence. Reuse an exact existing admission if it covers this contract; this document is not admission. [S1-01, S1-10–S1-11; DIRECT]

Produce one repair candidate for `/fictional/seed-context/candidate/context_select.py`, plus focused checks in `/fictional/seed-context/candidate/test_context_select.py`. Requirements and accepted design `D-seed-2` stay unchanged. Permitted reads are this scenario brief, `/fictional/seed-context/specification/requirements.md`, `/fictional/seed-context/design/D-seed-2.md` and those two candidate files. Permitted effects are edits to those two files, focused in-memory Python checks and the run return at `/fictional/seed-context/work/run-8/RETURN.md`. No other project, Git, network, installation or publication operation is granted. No fictional path has been accessed by this generator. [S1-01, S1-08, S1-10]

`select_context(records, roots, budget)` accepts a finite list of uniquely identified records, root IDs and a nonnegative integer budget. Each record has a nonempty string `id`, a `requires` list of IDs and opaque JSON-compatible payload. Malformed types and duplicate record IDs are outside this task. Implement the finite visited-set/work-queue design and materialize whole records once, sorted by `id`; never mutate inputs. Keep every transitively required record regardless of standing. [S1-02, S1-04, S1-08]

The exact success is `{status: complete, records: [...]}`. A closure larger than budget returns exactly `{status: refused, reason: budget_exceeded, records: []}`. Unknown roots refuse with `unknown_root`; dangling dependencies refuse with `dangling_reference`, including dangling links anywhere in the supplied graph even outside the selected closure. Apply precedence `unknown_root`, then `dangling_reference`, then `budget_exceeded`. A valid empty-root graph at budget zero completes with an empty list. Cycles and duplicate paths are valid. [S1-05–S1-07]

Derive checks from those predicates and the accepted design, not from the implementation. Obtain actual failing-before/passing-after evidence where reproducible. At minimum distinguish: unresolved C retained in A→B,C; exact budget boundary versus refusal with no partial records; unknown-root priority over other failures; dangling reference in an unselected record; valid cycles and duplicate paths without duplication/nontermination; empty roots with both valid and globally dangling graphs; sorting, whole opaque payload and input preservation. The A/B/C example requires three records and budget at least three. These are supplied requirements and derived falsification targets, not prescribed implementation details or invented test observations. [S1-03–S1-08; WORK]

The old smoke at `seed-r7` covers only a resolved leaf. Record it as historical, not successor proof. A result can be reused only for the same applicable subject/basis/support; material changes or revising observations invalidate affected reliance. Do not require an independent review or durable ticket merely to return this run-local repair. [S1-09, S1-11; REUSE; REVIEW]

Return to the owner through `run-8/RETURN.md`: exact predecessor/successor candidate identities, changed paths, contract/admission binding, actual check inputs/results and their limits, unchanged requirement/design, self-review, remaining uncertainty and any unresolved obligation. `candidate_ready` means a proposed candidate with evidence, not accepted. A real activation refusal is distinct from a Worker result; otherwise return a bounded refusal/incomplete/re-entry result if the grant or evidence cannot support the candidate. Never manufacture observations. Stop after the return; request the owner's exact re-entry for any material boundary change. [S1-12; WORK]

'''+sources
reviewer='''# S1: inactive proposed Reviewer context

Status: inactive and conditional. S1-11 imposes no independent-review condition; a direct Writer's self-review is sufficient evidence for the owner's bounded decision where applicable. No candidate or review yet exists. This document does not create an assessment grant, ticket or mandatory gate. [S1-09, S1-11; REVIEW]

If the owner later grants review of the exact successor candidate returned in `/fictional/seed-context/work/run-8/RETURN.md`, apply released `stdo-review`. First bind its candidate identity/checkpoint, Product Definition and exact basis, claim, permitted evidence population, capability, selected severity policy and return/write grant. These later review coordinates are unavailable now. The existing Writer grant is not a Reviewer grant. Until they are supplied, do not inspect a fictional candidate or write a report. [S1-10–S1-12; REVIEW]

The claim would be that the candidate satisfies S1-02 and S1-04–S1-08 under unchanged requirement and `D-seed-2`: complete finite transitive closure, whole records once sorted by ID, standing-independent retention, input preservation, exact success/refusal shape, globally checked dangling references, refusal precedence, valid cycles/duplicate paths and empty-root behavior. Malformed types and duplicate record IDs remain excluded. Derive an expectation set from the governing requirements/design before candidate inspection. The supplied diagnosis and illustrative A/B/C graph are inputs, not a requested verdict. Independently seek counterexamples including unselected dangling links and simultaneous refusal causes. [S1-02–S1-08; released stdo-review / Choose The Entry and Evaluate]

Acquire the exact authorized source, candidate, test source and actual observations directly; a Worker summary does not replace evidence. The old smoke proves only its resolved-leaf case at `seed-r7`. Assess input/effect semantics and retained alternatives across this local function's complete path. [S1-09; WORK; REUSE]

This generator has seen the brief and authored the proposed contexts; it has performed no assessment. A later Reviewer must disclose its actual prior exposure and authorship. Required independence needs a non-author, independently acquired evidence/expectations and the governing actor-family policy; a fresh session or role label is insufficient, and absent a stated policy two same-model-family activations are not semantically independent. Reporting defects alone is not authorship; adopted repair/design wording is. [INDEPENDENCE]

If lawfully activated, the candidate remains read-only. No repair, priority assignment, acceptance, publication or next activation follows. Return to the owner through the then-named authorized review channel; no review-result path or report write is currently granted. Use a closed `satisfied`, `falsified`, `indeterminate`, `out_of_frame` or `invalid_basis` evaluation with exact subject/basis, claim, scope/exclusions, evidence, findings/counterexamples, residuals, uncertainty and re-entry. Each finding identifies a violated property, supported entry/state and causal path; use only the Product-selected severity scale, leaving unavailable fields explicit. `satisfied` and `invalid_basis` have triage `not_applicable`; falsified findings have supported triage or field-level indeterminacy. Preserve unperformed coverage and stop. Material candidate/basis/evidence/independence changes invalidate affected reliance. No verdict is prescribed here. [REVIEW; REUSE; released stdo-review / Return]

'''+sources
